I'm having my best game ever. Great luck in the mines: found a BoH and a
temple to Huan Ti and  a black unicorn with a fondness for emeralds in
minetown, a polymorph trap that turned my large cat into a disenchanter
the level below, and a bunch of good spellbooks in the catecombs. (Of
course, down in the catecombs there was also another polymorph trap, which
turned my disenchanter into... a housecat.) I made a mistake praying for
holy water after tossing too many gems, so got crowned, but made enough to
keep making more.

After getting the AoR and studying all my spellbooks in Sokoban I went
back to the mines, Offered a bunch of corpses (which yielded only
Orcrist), beat up on a chickatrice and thought hmmmm.... Poor Izchak and
all the other shopkeepers. Between their pocket change, a leprechaun hall,
and a bones file I had enough cash to get my bare AC down to 1. My monk
knew about 15 spells thanks to the minetown shops, including ID, so
magic-wise life was very very sweet. I experimented with polypiling, but
somehow couldn't find a robe at all. I'm still completely wishless,
genoless, and vegetarian however. I goofed on wielded, though, with a dumb
pickaxe moment.

Not advanced enough yet to do the quest, I started meandering down until
I found a titan casting create monster all over. Not an opportunity - a
big retreat. But in falling back to a more manageable lvl 18 I found a
vault with the entrance to Fort Ludios. This is the first time I'd *ever*
found it. Now I'll admit to looking at the gazetteer, but I didn't use
Elbereth for anything but the protection of my loot pile. I managed it
with -17AC, a pair of beartraps for traffic management, and three dozen
blessed poisoned +5 darts. :)

I was a Student of Waters before I had to face Croesus, or even the four
dragons in the moat. Got silver, blue, and black scale, about 46K in gold,
more wants of create monster than I could shake YA wand at (please let
there be a coaligned altar soon), and enough phat lewt that a blessed BoH
was going to be a stress to carry. QED: Burn Elbereth, lock the door,
name one sack "cache" and the BoH "carry". 

And in the process, I put an unnamed sack containing two wands of
canellation into the BoH. Do not pass go, so not collect 46000 Zorkmids,
12 potions of holy water, two magic markers and 17 blessed blank scrolls,
or all the C-Rations I could ever care to want to eat.

*sigh*. Well, I thought I was going to need more practice before I faced
Master Kaen anyhow. 


